RT by @RepFedorchak: “The losses we are experiencing are staggering and unsustainable. Our farms and factories won’t be able to hold on much longer if the U.S. cannot control the artificially and destructively cheap foreign sugar imports that are undercutting American-made sugar,” says Brent Baldwin, a fourth-generation sugarbeet farmer from St. Thomas, North Dakota.

